# The Alchemy Railway context upload reads `.dockerignore` (after
# `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, if present) — it never reads `.railwayignore`,
# which stays for manual `railway up` runs. The upload caps the tar at
# 32 MiB and 10,000 entries, and rejects symlinks anywhere it includes, so
# everything the Railpack build of `apps/server` and `apps/web` does not
# read stays out: local-only dirs, build outputs, secrets, and the drizzle
# snapshot history (drizzle-kit migrate reads the journal, which stays;
# the per-migration snapshots serve generate/check on a full checkout).

# Version control, CI, agent machinery
.git
.github
.agents
AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
.claude
.codex
.warden
.wayfinder
.teach
.campaign
.loop
.artifacts
.jscpd
.vscode

# Local-only content
docs
references
archive
.handoff
.lessons
.tmp-screens
.tmp
.scratch-*
.vsnap*
teaching
logs
*.log
PRD.md
plan.md
progress.txt
*-plan.md
*-progress.txt
*-loop.sh
ralph.sh

# Dependencies and build outputs
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store
coverage
.nyc_output
.cache
tmp
temp
*.tgz

# Secrets never ride the upload
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Drizzle snapshot history (the journal stays)
packages/db/src/migrations/meta/*_snapshot.json

# OS noise
.DS_Store
